WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Bias is not a moral failure or proof that someone is careless.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.850
In critical thinking,

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.810
bias means a predictable judgment tendency that can shape how people notice evidence,

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.985
interpret it, and decide what to do.

00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:14.010
Because bias is common, the useful question is not who has bias.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.899
The useful question is what process helps us reduce avoidable distortion.

00:00:17.899 --> 00:00:21.965
Confirmation bias is the tendency to favor information that supports an existing belief or

00:00:21.965 --> 00:00:22.620
hypothesis.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.485
In security work,

00:00:23.485 --> 00:00:27.820
an analyst may focus on evidence that confirms an early theory about an incident.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:28.500
In leadership,

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.110
a manager may notice examples that support a view about a team while missing contrary

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:32.800
evidence.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.650
The countermeasure is to ask what evidence would change our mind and what alternative

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.400
explanation also fits the facts.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.900
Anchoring makes an initial number, diagnosis, or opinion exert too much influence.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.230
Availability makes recent or vivid examples feel more likely than they are.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.800
Overconfidence makes people stop checking too early.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.150
Sunk cost makes it hard to abandon a weak path because time, money,

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.352
or reputation has already been invested.

00:00:54.352 --> 00:00:57.880
Motivated reasoning pulls analysis toward the answer people want to be true.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.640
Groupthink adds social pressure.

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.320
Teams may avoid disagreement because they want harmony, speed,

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.270
or approval from senior people.

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:07.185
A group can become confident because everyone is repeating the same assumption,

00:01:07.185 --> 00:01:08.960
not because the evidence is strong.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.555
That is why structured review is valuable.

00:01:10.555 --> 00:01:14.670
It gives permission to surface alternatives before commitment becomes expensive.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.005
Bias reduction does not require perfect rationality.

00:01:17.005 --> 00:01:21.565
Practical methods include checklists, independent review, alternative hypotheses,

00:01:21.565 --> 00:01:24.440
pre-mortems, explicit assumptions, and evidence checks.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.280
The goal is not to remove human judgment.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.370
The goal is to support judgment with habits that make reasoning more visible and

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.120
correctable.
